","F.R.Brown.2","P.Bacilieri.2","N.Ishizuka.1","B.A.Berg.1","L.Wu.2","S.Necco.1","P.Giacomelli.1","A.Billoire.1","M.Creutz.1","M.Guagnelli.1","Shinji.Hioki.1","R.Tripiccione.1","F.Marzano.1","H.Wittig.1","Norman.H.Christ.1","L.Karkkainen.1","D.Toussaint.1","N.Tsutsui.1","U.M.Heller.1","G.Fiorentini.1","E.Remiddi.1","F.Niedermayer.1","G.Schierholz.1","M.Okuda.3","C.Cristian.1","M.Albanese.1","S.Aoki.1","Takaaki.Hashimoto.1","L.Susskind.1","C.Morningstar.1","A.C.Irving.1","K.N.Orginos.1","D.Weingarten.1","P.Weisz.1","F.Karsch.1","P.Rufenacht.2","A.Peikert.1","M.Fukugita.1","H.B.Meyer.1","Juergen.Engels.1","F.Rapuano.1","K.Jansen.1","N.Cabibbo.1","A.Nakamura.1","M.P.Lombardo.1","R.Wohlert.1","K.Kanaya.1","P.Hasenfratz.1","Yasumichi.Aoki.1","R.G.Edwards.1","S.Tominaga.8","T.Manke.2","E.Marinari.1","M.Bernaschi.1","M.Okamoto.1","S.Cabasino.2","Yoshihito.Iwasaki.1","H.Matsufuru.1","R.Petronzio.1","Shigemi.Ohta.1","D.W.Bliss.4","A.A.Khan.4","M.Luscher.1","M.Fujisaki.1","E.Laermann.1","N.Yamada.1","Robert.D.Mawhinney.1","F.Costantini.1","Kei-ichi.Nagai.1","C.Dawson.1","A.M.Polyakov.1","Y.Tago.2","M.Okawa.1","P.W.Stephenson.2","G.C.Liu.2","Takashi.Kaneko.1","I.O.Stamatescu.1","M.Garcia.Perez.1","G.S.Bali.1","Graham.Boyd.1","K.Rummukainen.1","G.Parisi.1","P.Marchesini.22","P.Paolucci.1","R.Sommer.1","R.Burkhalter.1","U.Wolff.1","C.E.Detar.1","K.I.Ishikawa.1","T.J.Woch.2","Osamu.Miyamura.1","M.J.Peardon.1","Takayuki.Umeda.1","L.Fonti.2","S.Petrarca.1","A.Huntley.1","B.Beinlich.1","M.Teper.1","Thomas.C.Blum.1","Y.Kuramashi.1","G.P.Lepage.1","B.Petersson.1"],"legacy_version":"20160523182153.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Lattice"}],"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/01js2sh04"}],"full_name":"Necco, Silvia","last_name":"Necco","first_name":"Silvia","recid":1020628},"control_number":627334,"dois":[{"value":"10.1016/j.nuclphysb.2004.01.032"}],"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Necco:2003vh"],"abstracts":[{"value":"We study universality and scaling properties of RG gauge actions (Iwasaki and DBW2). In the first part we consider the critical temperature T_{c} and compute the reference energy scale r_{0} for critical couplings \\beta_{c} corresponding to N_{t}=3,4,6,8. The universality of T_{c}r_{0} between Iwasaki and Wilson action is confirmed and the scaling behavior of the Iwasaki action is found to be better than the one for the Wilson action. The results for the DBW2 action show larger lattice artefacts. A continuum value T_{c}r_{0}=0.7498(50) is extracted. We compute also the glueball masses for the states 0^{++} and 2^{++}, investigate the scaling of m_{0^{++}}r_{0} and m_{2^{++}}r_{0} and point out practical problems which are due to the violation of positivity present in the RG actions."},{"source":"Elsevier","value":"We study universality and scaling properties of RG gauge actions (Iwasaki and DBW2). In the first part we consider the critical temperature T c and compute the reference energy scale r 0 for critical couplings β c corresponding to N t =3,4,6,8. The universality of T c r 0 between Iwasaki and Wilson action is confirmed and the scaling behavior of the Iwasaki action is found to be better than the one for the Wilson action. The results for the DBW2 action show larger lattice artifacts. A continuum value T c r 0 =0.7498(50) is extracted. We compute also the glueball masses for the states 0 ++ and 2 ++ , investigate the scaling of m 0 ++ r 0 and m 2 ++ r 0 and point out practical problems which are due to the violation of positivity present in the RG actions.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Elsevier"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["hep-lat"],"titles":[{"title":"Universality and scaling behavior of RG gauge actions"},{"title":"Renormalization group"},{"source":"arXiv","title":"Universality and scaling behavior of RG gauge actions."}],"curated":true},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/627334?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A627334"},"id":"627334","updated":"2023-03-06T13:47:09.319594+00:00"},{"created":"2025-10-03T08:24:47.876327+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":8,"authors":[{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"deng, shusa","full_name":"Deng, Shusa","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1389231"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Shu.Sen.Deng.1"}],"last_name":"Deng","first_name":"Shusa","uuid":"bc989e66-fcf7-4a8a-bcd9-e28d4e24f9c5","recid":1389231},{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"ortiz, gerardo","full_name":"Ortiz, Gerardo","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/994757"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Gerardo.Ortiz.1"}],"last_name":"Ortiz","first_name":"Gerardo","uuid":"9a3578b8-0e42-4ec3-b327-37c83fe2414e","recid":994757},{"full_name_unicode_normalized":"viola, lorenza","full_name":"Viola, Lorenza","record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/authors/1988640"},"ids":[{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"L.Viola.3"}],"last_name":"Viola","first_name":"Lorenza","uuid":"150bcd02-d05a-4549-b9c4-8aaa6a428174","recid":1988640}],"citation_count_without_self_citations":5,"citeable":true,"$schema":"https://inspirehep.net/schemas/records/hep.json","references":[{"reference":{"label":"1","publication_info":{"year":1999},"misc":["Quantum Phase Transitions (Cambridge UP, Cambridge,)"],"authors":[{"full_name":"Sachdev, S."}]},"raw_refs":[{"schema":"text","source":"arXiv","value":"1. S. Sachdev, Quantum Phase Transitions (Cambridge UP, Cambridge, 1999)."}]},{"reference":{"label":"2","publication_info":{"journal_volume":"415","artid":"39","year":2002,"page_start":"39","journal_