:"Using direct mass measurements and different MCRG methods we investigated the onset of asymptotic scaling and the universality of the mass gap. The standard nearest-neighbour action and a modified action with next-to-nearest neighbour coupling were studied up to correlation length ξ ∼ 1090 and ξ ∼ 330, respectively. The different methods give consistently that asymptotic scaling sets in only above ξ ∼ 500 for the standard action, while much earlier, at ξ ∼ 40, for the modified one. In full agreement with universality, the results m = (3.3 ± 0.1)Λ MS and m = (3.4 ± 0.1)Λ MS were obtained for these two cases, respectively.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"Elsevier"}}],"titles":[{"title":"Mass Gap, Scaling and Universality in the $d=2$ O(3) $\\sigma$ Model"},{"title":"MASS GAP, SCALING AND UNIVERSALITY IN THE d = 2 O(3) sigma MODEL"}],"imprints":[{"date":"1990"}],"curated":true},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/285244?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A285244"},"id":"285244","updated":"2023-03-06T17:05:36.441223+00:00"},{"created":"2025-06-16T15:53:27.255165+00:00","metadata":{"citation_count":207,"authors":[{"raw_affiliations":[{"value":"Institute for Quantum Optics and Quantum Information of the Austrian Academy of Sciences, 6020 Innsbruck, Austria"},{"value":"Institute for Theoretical Physics, University of Innsbruck, 6020 Innsbruck, Austria"},{"value":"Physik Department, Technische Universität München, 85747 Garching, Germany"}],"full_name_unicode_normalized":"heyl, markus","full_name":"Heyl, Markus","record":{"$ref":"https://insp